I shipped only half of this task. The yoagent bump to 0.24.1 is in. Routing piped -p output through retry_safe_events is not, because wiring it broke two existing tests by losing text.

Step 1, the bump (commit `1699b725`):
• Only `Cargo.lock changed for the dependency. The same update also moved some windows-sys` entries from 0.61.2 to 0.59.0, which I didn't revert. They don't matter on Linux, but they're in the diff.
• `tests/doc_version_claims.rs` checks every version marker in the repo, not just the one in CLAUDE.md. So I moved all 14 markers to 0.24.1 and left the surrounding text alone. Between 0.24.0 and 0.24.1 only two yoagent files changed, retry.rs and agent_loop.rs, and none of the marked statements are about those changes.
• The `retry after {retry_after_ms:?}ms` message (the "Nonems" leak) is unchanged: that yoagent file is byte-identical between the two versions.
• `cargo build, cargo test`, clippy and fmt all pass.

What the filter does: it holds back each attempt's streamed text and releases it only if the attempt succeeds. An attempt that gets retried disappears, so only the retry notice comes through. An attempt that fails for good comes through as its start and error-end events without its text, although the text is still inside the error-end message.

Step 2, the wiring, measured and reverted (commit `32284edc` records why):
• **Retry succeeds:** before, stdout was `PARTIAL_\n` with 1 request and a nonzero exit (the #989 abort). After, it was `PONG\n` with 2 requests and exit 0, which is what the task wanted.
• **Retry never succeeds:** the partial text was not duplicated and the exit was nonzero, also as wanted.
• **The problem:** when a turn dies for good on an error yoagent doesn't retry, stdout was now empty. The partial answer that `print_mode_keeps_partial_answer_when_turn_dies_mid_stream` and its sibling test protect was lost. Because nothing counted as already printed, yoyo's own retry also fired 6 times.
• **A second problem:** I first wrapped at `start_prompt`, which also caught the stream-json output. That broke how stream-json marks a failed attempt, so the wrap has to go in run_prompt_once* instead.

This is close to the task's stated fallback condition (filter can't be used on the text path) but not exactly the wording I was given: the filter doesn't drop the end event, it drops the text inside it. The fix is clear: when the filter has held back an attempt's text, print it from the error-end message, then wrap at run_prompt_once*. I didn't attempt it because I was past my token budget, and shipping the wiring as it stood would have broken a guarantee the tests pin. The 15-site guard in src/prompt.rs didn't need changing: my wiring added no new text-printing sites, and it's now reverted anyway.

#991: I posted the comment with both commits, the before/after numbers and the open questions, and confirmed it shows in gh issue view 991 --comments. The issue stays open. Not probed yet:
• the abort racing a zero or tiny backoff;
• `classify_stop_reason and fatal_error` when no second end event arrives;
• whether the filter would remove the stream-json collected_text duplication;
• "Ok without Done". 0.24.1 now closes that message itself, but I haven't checked it from yoyo.
